15048	{"artifactId":"LLD-d9f85b3cc8cc966b-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-d9f85b3cc8cc966b-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:40:12.909Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every element of the SPEC intent is designed: a header (project name with an optional .insrc override, title, type badge, Work item, Source doc replacing the back-link, an injected date, git user with an OS fallback); a context line plus an optional narrative; one transform pan/zoom with toolbar and fit-on-load for all four visuals; the per-type tables (ER entities and columns, UX key elements with markers, sequence participants and messages, component path); erDiagram; labelled, autonumbered sequence arrows with dashed returns; and optional descriptions that raise LOW findings.","evidence":"SPEC-77932eaa1a85819b.json body.intent and scopeBoundary list exactly these items. The LLD covers each one: header in §3.1, content and tables in §3.2, schemas in §3.3–3.6, LOW findings in §3.7, pan/zoom shell in §7.1, and ER/sequence fixes in §2.1 and §2.3. SequenceMessage already has `kind?: 'call'|'return'|'recurse'` (sequence.ts:43), so dashed returns can be derived. Component already has a `label`, and the LLD adds `path` as the SPEC requires. [files: .insrc/artifacts/SPEC-77932eaa1a85819b.json, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/sequence.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No SPEC non-goal is built: existing docs/ companions are not migrated, no new visual types are added, no pan/zoom differs per type, and narrative and descriptions are not made required.","evidence":"SPEC nonGoals list these four. The LLD Migration section says 'Existing committed companions stay in the old format'. It keeps the same four kinds, uses one panzoom.js for every page, and makes every new field optional, with completenessFindings LOW only and the validators unchanged. [files: .insrc/artifacts/SPEC-77932eaa1a85819b.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the ER, sequence and component companions render through docgen assembleShell via the *DefinitionToIr lowerings and withSourceLink. The UX companion renders through renderUxMockDocument with no pan/zoom.","evidence":"render.ts:90-91 `const ir = withSourceLink(erDefinitionToIr(erDef), opts.sourceLink); const outcome = await assembleShell(ir);`, and the same pattern at :191 and :229. render.ts:150 `const html = renderUxMockDocument(uxDef, title, { sourceLink: opts.sourceLink });`. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The finalize helpers swallow only DiagramGenerationError, rethrow anything else, and run after the HIGH validation gate (firstCompanionValidationFailure).","evidence":"orchestrator.ts:1620-1625 `if (err instanceof DiagramGenerationError) { log.warn(...); return undefined; } throw err;`. The same applies for UX (1653-1658) and sequence/component (1693-1712). firstCompanionValidationFailure (around 1560-1584) validates all four definitions before rendering. [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"generateErCompanions has no production caller; only its test calls it.","evidence":"Searching non-test src for `generateErCompanions` finds only its definition in generate.ts:62 and its doc comment. The only other hits are __tests__/generate.test.ts. The production renderErCompanion callers are orchestrator.ts:1619 and generate.ts:99. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/generate.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused header inputs exist in the stated shape: safeCanonical and the epic/story workflow-id minters in id.ts, `<repo>/.insrc/config.json` as a project config file, and the standalone story title stored in boundary.internal from params.storyTitle.","evidence":"id.ts:146 `epicWorkflowId(epicHash, createdAtISO)`, :150 `storyWorkflowId(...)`, :185 `safeCanonical(mint: () => WorkflowId): string | undefined`, :202 `deriveWorkItemIdentity`. repo-ignore-config.ts:39-41 resolves `<repo>/.insrc/config.json`. standalone.ts:48 `const title = strParam(params, 'storyTitle') ?? focus;` and :65 `boundary: { storyId, owns: [], depends: [], internal: title }`. [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/indexer/repo-ignore-config.ts, src/workflow/runners/design-story/standalone.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The epic-Story LLD finalize already resolves the Epic's DEF and the Story, so the context line can reuse it without a new read. The UX card emitter already escapes its output.","evidence":"orchestrator.ts:2110 `const epic = requireApprovedEpic(intent.repoPath, epicHash);` and :2113 `const story = epic.body.stories.find(s => s.id === storyId);` inside finalizeDesignStory (2062). ux.ts calls escaping helpers 17 times. [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/ux.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are exactly three finalize sites (HLD, epic-Story LLD, standalone LLD). Each calls the ER, UX and diagram helpers, and these helpers plus the dead generate.ts seam are the only production callers of render*Companion.","evidence":"orchestrator.ts:1834/1837/1840 (finalizeDesignEpic), 2190/2192/2195 (finalizeDesignStory) and 2364/2366/2369 (finalizeStandaloneLld). The helpers call render*Companion at 1619, 1652, 1692 and 1705. The only other non-test caller is generate.ts:99. [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/generate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test inventory (§3.9) is complete: it lists every suite that calls render*Companion or imports the removed lowerings, renderUxMockDocument or generateErCompanions.","evidence":"Test files that reference *DefinitionToIr, renderUxMockDocument, generateErCompanions, sourceLink or the back-link text: component, context-sections, er, fixtures/er-parity, generate, sequence, ux-mock-render, ux, and src/workflow/__tests__/companion-context-finalize.test.ts. All are in the inventory. Suites calling render*Companion (render, diagram-render, ux-render, ux-integration) are also listed. The code-review tests (dimensions/__tests__/diagram.test.ts, ux.test.ts, diagram-conditional, ux-conditional, mcp ux-handler) import only types, adherence or validators, so they are unaffected. docgen narrative-band.test.ts stays because docgen is unchanged. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/__tests__, src/workflow/__tests__/companion-context-finalize.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/diagram.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"validateErDefinition and validateUxDefinition validate against closed vendored schemas, so those schema assets must gain the new fields or every described definition fails with HIGH.","evidence":"linkml-metamodel.schema.json has `\"additionalProperties\": false` at the root (line 5), on ErClass (21) and on ErSlot (33), with no description or narrative property. adaptive-cards.schema.json has 12 `additionalProperties: false` occurrences, including the root (line 5, properties only type/version/body). metamodel.ts:33 and adaptive-cards.ts:35 load these assets. The LLD §3.3/§3.6 extends both. [files: src/assets/artifacts/schemas/linkml-metamodel.schema.json, src/assets/artifacts/schemas/adaptive-cards.schema.json, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/metamodel.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/adaptive-cards.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Stored sequence and component definitions stay valid, and described ones pass: their validators are hand-written and ignore unknown keys, so only the closed *_PROPERTY_SCHEMA objects need the new fields.","evidence":"sequence.ts:93-154 validateSequenceDefinition checks only that participants and messages are arrays, that ids are non-empty and unique, that from/to/label are present, and referential integrity. It does not reject extra keys. sequence-schema.ts:26/34/46/61 and component-schema.ts:26/34/46 are `additionalProperties: false`, which the LLD updates (§3.4/§3.5). [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/sequence.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/sequence-schema.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/component-schema.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"UX_DEFINITION_PROPERTY_SCHEMA needs only a root `narrative`, because its body items are loose; element and action descriptions live in the vendored asset.","evidence":"ux-schema.ts:24-35: root `additionalProperties: false` with properties type/version/body and `body: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object' } }`. Items are loose, so element-level `description` passes this schema. Actions exist only inside ActionSet (ux.ts:102-104 `readonly actions: readonly UxAction[]`), which sits under body. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/ux-schema.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/ux.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The docgen tool stays untouched: generateDocument still calls assembleShell, and companions stop importing it rather than changing it.","evidence":"docgen/index.ts:32 imports assembleShell, and :118 `return assembleShell(ir.value);`. Companion code reaches docgen only through render.ts:22-23 (assembleShell and the DocumentIR type), which the LLD removes. No change to src/docgen is in the change-site lists. This is a standalone Story (no HLD or sibling Stories), so docgen is the only shared surface. [files: src/docgen/index.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A missing pan/zoom or Mermaid asset is caught. A new src/assets/artifacts/companion/panzoom.js ships to out/assets through the existing copy step, and throwing DiagramGenerationError, including from the UX path, is swallowed by finalize.","evidence":"copy-assets.mjs:28-39 recursively copies all of `src/assets` to `out/assets` (`cpSync(src, dst, { recursive: true })`), so a new asset ships with no script change. orchestrator.ts:1654 already catches DiagramGenerationError for UX, and 1621/1694/1707 catch it for the others. docgen shell.ts:259-265 shows the same pattern for a failed runtime load. [files: copy-assets.mjs, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/docgen/render/shell.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Removing the *DefinitionToIr lowerings keeps finalize from aborting. The lowerings throw their own non-DiagramGenerationError errors (ErDefinition/SequenceDefinitionError/ComponentDefinitionError) on dangling references, which finalize would rethrow. The LLD does not say how the new page builders handle a dangling endpoint.","evidence":"sequence.ts:258-274 and component.ts:222-225 throw *DefinitionError on undeclared endpoints, and finalize rethrows non-DiagramGenerationError (orchestrator.ts:1625/1697/1710). However, validateSequenceDefinition (sequence.ts:130-150) and the component and ER validators already flag dangling references as HIGH, and firstCompanionValidationFailure gates on them before any render. The builders therefore never see such input. The LLD's preconditions ('passed firstCompanionValidationFailure') state this. Not stated: whether builders keep the defense-in-depth throw; a builder should not need one. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/sequence.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/component.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"Optional: say in §2 whether the page builders keep the defense-in-depth dangling-endpoint check, and if so which error they throw.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each LLD acceptance criterion (ac1–ac7, derived from the SPEC because a standalone Story has no Epic ACs) maps to at least one named test, including the closed-schema extension, the header fallbacks and docgen no-regression.","evidence":"The §5 acceptance mapping covers each criterion. ac1: shell order plus finalize header plus contextLine. ac2: one runtime, no URL, toolbar. ac3: ER builder. ac4: sequence builder. ac5: validators with descriptions plus completenessFindings plus code-review LOWs. ac6: header fallbacks. ac7: docgen shell.test.ts. The validator test proves the vendored schemas were extended (needed per linkml-metamodel.schema.json:5/21/33). The docgen suite exists under src/docgen/render/__tests__. The SPEC has no explicit AC ids (body.decisions and openItems are empty), as the LLD's open question ts1 notes. [files: .insrc/artifacts/SPEC-77932eaa1a85819b.json, src/assets/artifacts/schemas/linkml-metamodel.schema.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-11T10:40:12.909Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
